{"path":"\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/' data-target='root' data-title=''>&#8962; <\/a>\r\n\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer' data-target='computer' data-title='Computer'>\r\n\t\t\tComputer\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer\/os' data-target='computer\/os' data-title='OS'>\r\n\t\t\tOS\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer\/os\/nix' data-target='computer\/os\/nix' data-title='*Nix'>\r\n\t\t\t*Nix\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu' data-target='computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu' data-title='Ubuntu'>\r\n\t\t\tUbuntu\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n","async":"0","desc":"apt-get update, upgrade, dist-upgrade, do-release-upgrade, and rebuilding apt lists.","label":"Update","prevArticle":{"id":"computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu\/service","label":"Service","url":"\/computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu\/service"},"nextArticle":{"id":"computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu\/version","label":"Version","url":"\/computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu\/version"},"languageSwitcher":"<div id='language-switcher'>\n<\/div>\n","content":"<div id='message'>\n\t<h2>Package lists and upgrades<\/h2>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>apt-get update<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<p>\n\t\tGets the update list.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>apt-get upgrade<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<p>\n\t\tApplies the update.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>apt-get dist-upgrade<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<p>\n\t\tUpgrades packages. Dangerous: it will force installation of new packages and remove old packages. For non-auto-updating packages, it intelligently updates dependency packages.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>apt full upgrade<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<p>\n\t\tPerforms all of the above.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>apt autoremove<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<p>\n\t\tRemoves lingering packages.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>apt --fix-broken install<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>apt-get update &amp;&amp; apt-get upgrade<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<p>\n\t\tCaution: <code class='inline'>dist-upgrade<\/code> can install new packages and remove old ones.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<h2>Major update<\/h2>\n\t<p>\n\t\tExample: 12 &gt; 14.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>do-release-upgrade<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>apt-get install update-manager-core<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<p>\n\t\tAlternate SSH \u2014 open port 1022:\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>iptables -I INPUT -p tcp --dport 1022 -j ACCEPT<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<p>\n\t\tMay throw: bad network or server error.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<h2>Repair lists<\/h2>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>apt-get clean\ncd \/var\/lib\/apt\nmv lists lists.old\nmkdir -p lists\/partial\napt-get clean\napt-get update<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<h2>Release upgrades file<\/h2>\n\t<p>\n\t\t<code class='inline'>\/etc\/update-manager\/release-upgrades<\/code> values: <code class='inline'>normal<\/code> | <code class='inline'>lts<\/code> | <code class='inline'>off<\/code>.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<h2>Message<\/h2>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>\/var\/lib\/ubuntu-release-upgrader\/release-upgrade-available<\/code><\/pre>\n<\/div>\n\n<div id='updated-container'>\r\n\t<div id='updated'>\r\n\t\tUpdated:\r\n\t\t<span id='date'>\r\n\t\t\t2026 Aug 19\t\t<\/span>\r\n\t<\/div>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<div class='center' id='content-body-separator'><\/div>\r\n<div id='sub-list' class='center page-list'>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<div id='fb_components'>\r\n\t<div class=\"fb-comments\"\n  data-href=\"https:\/\/ujnotes.com\/computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu\/update\"\n  data-numposts=\"50\">\n<\/div>\n\t<div class=\"fb-like\"\n  data-href=\"https:\/\/ujnotes.com\/computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu\/update\"\n  data-layout=\"button\"\n  data-action=\"like\"\n  data-size=\"small\"\n  data-show-faces=\"false\"\n  data-share=\"true\">\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\r\n<div id='nav-list' class='center page-list'>\r\n\t<a id='nav-menu-prev'\r\n\t\t\tclass='XURL item_block_container' href='\/computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu\/service' data-target='computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu\/service' data-title='Service' >\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image item_block_image_visible' src='\/resource\/placeholder.svg' loading='lazy' alt='Navigation - previous page tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div class='arrow'>&#x25C4;<\/div><div>Service<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t\t<\/a><a id='nav-menu-next'\r\n\t\t\tclass='XURL item_block_container' href='\/computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu\/version' data-target='computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu\/version' data-title='Version' >\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image item_block_image_visible' src='\/resource\/placeholder.svg' loading='lazy' alt='Navigation - next page tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div>Version<\/div><div class='arrow'>&#x25BA;<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t\t<\/a><a id='nav-menu-up' class='XURL item_block_container ' href='\/computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu' data-target='computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu' data-title='Ubuntu'>\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image ' loading='lazy' src='\/computer\/os\/nix\/ubuntu.svg ' alt='Navigation - up level tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div>Ubuntu<\/div><div class='arrow'>&#x25B2;<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t<\/a> <\/div>\r\n"}